WEBVTT

00:05:29.341 --> 00:05:30.853
down at those sorts of depths.

00:05:30.877 --> 00:05:33.214
We needed more time.
There had to be a better way.

00:05:33.238 --> 00:05:34.912
And indeed, there is a better way.

00:05:34.936 --> 00:05:37.096
In 1994, I was fortunate
enough to get access

00:05:37.120 --> 00:05:39.720
to these prototype
closed-circuit rebreathers.

00:05:40.527 --> 00:05:43.544
Closed-circuit rebreather:
what makes it different from scuba,

00:05:43.568 --> 00:05:44.729
and why is it better?

00:05:44.753 --> 00:05:47.604
Well, there are three main
advantages to a rebreather.

00:05:47.628 --> 00:05:49.788
One, they're quiet,
they don't make any noise.

00:05:49.812 --> 00:05:51.977
Two, they allow you to stay
underwater longer.

00:05:52.001 --> 00:05:53.874
Three, they allow you to go deeper.

00:05:53.898 --> 00:05:55.255
How is it that they do that?

00:05:55.279 --> 00:05:57.486
In order to really understand
how they do that,

00:05:57.510 --> 00:06:00.399
you have to look underneath the hood
and see what's going on.